one of the biggest surprises to come out  of the hogwarts legacy state of play  event just a few short months ago  actually happened just after the event  and that was the confirmation from  avalanche that hogwarts legacy is coming  to the nintendo switch now i won't  personally be playing the switch version  but i was super pumped about this i know  there's a lot of folks out there who  don't have a next-gen console or they  just prefer the switch the on-the-go  nature of it i get it now here's the  interesting piece of this not a lot of  fanfare was made about this avalanche  did not talk about it at the state of  play event at all which i guess kind of  makes sense considering it's a sony  event but even after very little mention  it actually popped up on an amazon  listing where you could pre-order the  game and then it would later appear on  the official website where we still have  the logo today stating that it is in  fact coming to hogwarts legacy as well  as in the faq section of the website as  well now here's where things get  interesting because even though hogwarts  legacy is being developed as a crosston  title spanning ps4 xbox one generation  along with the current gen ps5 and xbox  series x generation many myself included  were pretty surprised to see hogwarts  actually coming to the switch primarily  due to the console's outdated hardware  now it certainly makes sense from a  business perspective right i mean you  just take a look at the insane sales of  the switch that is a huge install base  right there and hogwarts legacy is  really going to make sure that it is  across every console imaginable no  matter which console you have there will  be a way to play this game but there's  one little thing one little issue here  that keeps popping up here on youtube  related to the switch version and it's  people who keep saying that hogwarts  legacy on switch will likely be a cloud  version of the game now yes i'm familiar  with cloud technology but honestly i had  no idea this was a thing on switch i  just kept seeing it over and over and so  i'm like okay what the heck is going on  here is this actually a thing that's  been happening on switch turns out it  totally is this nintendo life article  here from back in march has a list of  games that are currently available only  through the cloud on the nintendo switch  and you can see it's certainly not a  huge list but there are some big name  titles on here head on over to the  official nintendo site and you'll find a  lengthy explanation there about cloud  gaming on the switch but here's the  short version of it a cloud version of a  game uses streaming technology to play  the game from a server the cloud version  requires a stable connection to  high-speed internet to play because the  game is streamed from a server the full  software is not downloaded to your  nintendo switch system a small download  is required to launch the game okay so  if you're familiar with streaming  technology or if you've experimented  with it at all then you know it is very  hit and miss obviously it's incredibly  reliable incredibly dependent on your  internet connection but regardless even  with a great internet connection any  streaming that i have ever tried i have  always found the latency the input delay  from the controller to the cloud back to  my game is always just too long for me  to handle now it's certainly gotten  better over the years but for me  personally can't do it i have to have it  downloaded directly to my system not to  mention this causes a huge issue with  one of the main selling points of a  switch version and that's the idea of  the portability you would not be able to  play the cloud version let's say you're  on a plane ride without wi-fi or you're  riding in a car with no wi-fi or even if  you're just traveling from place to  place where you don't have a consistent  reliable internet connection then you  would not be able to play hogwarts  legacy if it ends up being a cloud  version of the game now on the positive  side of all this nintendo does give free  trials for all cloud titles which means  you can try before you actually fully  commit to purchasing the game when it  comes to hogwarts legacy though  considering how little they've said  about the switch version it does leave  me to wonder if this could be yet  another title that will be added to this  growing list of cloud only games for the  switch i mean if you go to amazon or  best buy or gamestop right now online  you can pre-order the switch version of  hogwarts legacy and there is no  reference to it being a cloud only title  who knows maybe that's a good sign maybe  the fact that it doesn't have that on  the listing they're already like hey  this is confirmed why why would it not  be a full version of the game now one  other thing that i double checked for a  lot of these titles that they have cloud  versions for is i looked on amazon to  see if they have a listing for any of  them with an actual picture of a game  box that you can order because if you  think about this if there's a cloud  version you'd essentially be ordering a  box that would have nothing but a code  in it now i have seen this done before  but when it comes to these switch cloud  versions at least in the titles i looked  for i could not find it so perhaps this  is a sign that we do already have  confirmation that the switch is going to  be a full-fledged version but if that's  the case i still can't figure out why  they just wouldn't outright say it and  frankly while we haven't heard more  about it but then the other side of this  that we also have to consider is the  fact that playstation certainly has some  sort of marketing exclusivity deal with  hogwarts legacy playstation is certainly  going to want to make it seem like their  version of the game is the absolute best  place to play and honestly that would  probably also explain why the switch  version has really been downplayed since  the announcement and you know what let's  explore that a little bit why do people  think it cannot be a full version well  it mainly goes back to what we were  talking about with the outdatedness of  the switch hardware then you throw in  the fact that hogwarts legacy is a fully  open world game it would certainly be a  challenge to run on the nintendo switch  now that being said titles like the  witcher i can't believe that this  actually happened but if you guys didn't  know this the witcher 3 actually was  ported to the nintendo switch and i  haven't played it myself but i've heard  it's actually not bad of course it's not  going to be what it was on pc or even on  the consoles but it was not bad all  things considered now the witcher is a  much older title than hogwarts legacy  even though it was very advanced  graphically for its time now not so much  so i totally get why this rumor has kind  of started i totally get why people are  asking this question i just hope we get  an answer from my avalanche fairly soon  on whether or not the switch version is  a cloud version or whether it is a  full-fledged port now i want to be  totally clear here this is a rumor there  is no confirmation of this whatsoever i  have reached out to community manager  chandler wood here on twitter and given  the reaction to this tweet how many of  you like this tweet even though it was  sent directly to him i think there's  clearly a group of people who want to  know information about this so hopefully  this video will be outdated very quickly  and we'll have a firm announcement on  this we'll have a firm answer to go by  and personally i really hope it comes  from avalanche sooner rather than later  because i know folks i know some of you  out there are currently trying to decide  which version of the game you want to  purchase now even if it is confirmed  that it is a full-fledged port then we  have to say okay well actually how does  it run how well does this game run we  did get confirmation that at least the  ps5 version will include both a fidelity  mode and a performance mode which is  certainly a good sign but if you are  someone out there who is looking at the  switch version of the game maybe you're  even thinking about pre-ordering the  switch version of the game personally i  would wait wait until we get official  confirmation from avalanche on how this  version of the game performs and whether  or not it is a full port or a cloud  version you know i don't always love  doing rumor videos but this is one of  those that i think is very important to  you the audience out there it's  important for you to know this  information when you're thinking about a  buying decision and whether or not the  switch version is something you want to  pick up i even know some people who have  been thinking about the switch is kind  of a second version so they'll have a  game to play while they're on the go as  well but this would certainly pose a  potential issue for  that and here lately the hogwarts legacy  news has just been rolling in week after  week if you didn't catch all the news  from the latest playstation blog post  and short video then check out the video  on the right side of your screen right  now as always thank you all so much for  watching i'll talk to you again soon
 

